{"id":1818,"date":"2020-12-08T02:42:27","date_gmt":"2020-12-08T10:42:27","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1818"},"modified":"2024-09-01T15:33:21","modified_gmt":"2024-09-01T22:33:21","slug":"codrone-python-library-and-driver-installation","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-python-library-and-driver-installation\/","title":{"rendered":"Driver Installation"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22156c0a07d\" name=\"6a22156c0a07d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Install driver<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To use your Bluetooth board with your computer, you need to download the correct USB driver. Click <a href=\"https:\/\/www.silabs.com\/developers\/usb-to-uart-bridge-vcp-drivers\">here<\/a> to go to the Silicon Labs downloads page and select the appropriate driver for your operating system.<\/p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION:<\/strong> The drivers for CoDrone Mini and CoDrone Lite\/Pro are <strong>different<\/strong>. Make sure you install from the links above if you are using CoDrone Lite\/Pro.<\/p>\n<p>Save the file to your desktop. When it&#8217;s finished downloading, extract\/unzip\/uncompress the file to a new folder, and then run the appropriate &#8216;CP210xVCPInstaller&#8217; for your operating system.<\/p>\n<p>If you&#8217;re on Windows, you can figure out if you&#8217;re using a x64 or x86 bit operating system by going to the start menu, right clicking This PC (or My Computer), and selecting Properties.<\/p>\n<p>Finally, run the installer. If everything&#8217;s successful, your driver should now be installed!<\/p>\n<p><strong>NOTE<\/strong>: If you are using a Windows device and the Silicon Labs driver that you installed from the link above does not work, try installing the version l